Minimum *SAT requirement is typically an 850 (Math + Critical Reading), but other factors can be taken into consideration. A number of programs have requirements for direct entry that are higher than university minimums. We advise checking the admission requirements for your program of interest within its designated section of the website. View our list of majors to find your program. *Note: Misericordia will be Test-Optional for Fall 2021 Admissions What type of financial aid is available? Misericordia offers merit-based scholarships for academics as well as community involvement, and need-based awards which can total well over $20,000 per year for qualified students. Visit our Financial Aid page to learn more . When should I apply? MU has a rolling admissions cycle, but we advise that students apply early in the cycle (Fall) as the space available in certain programs can be limited. Visit our Apply page to submit an application . Who can I contact with questions about my application? Your admissions counselor, or the Admissions Office at admiss@misericordia.edu or 1-866-262-6363. View our list of Admissions Staff to find your counselor. Career, Professional Development, & Leadership Mission Statement Our mission is to create inclusive and transformative learning experiences that empower students to thrive in an ever-changing professional world by providing resources, cultivating leadership, and developing the skills needed for professional success. We aim to foster lifelong professional growth through intentional support and meaningful opportunities. Office & Staff Insalaco Center for Professional Development and Leadership McAuley Hall 1st Floor, Room 106 301 Lake Street, Dallas, PA 18612 570-674-6409 | iccareer@misericordia.edu Office Hours: Monday through Friday 8:30 - 4:30 (4:00 May 11 - Aug 18) Bernadette (Bernie) Rushmer Director, Professional Development and Leadership 570-674-8028 | brushmer@misericordia.edu Tiffany Wiernusz Assistant Director, Professional Development and Leadership 570-674-6343 | twiernusz@misericordia.edu Johnna Evans, M.S. Corporate Relations Coordinator 570-674-6184 | jevans@misericordia.edu Janine Fawbush Administrative Assistant 570-674-6409 | jfawbush@misericordia.edu Career Center Spotlight See what’s happening at the Insalaco Center for Professional Development and Leadership. @misericordiau @Archie McGrowl stopped by the MU Career Center to get a new fit, develop a resume, mock interview and a new headshot #archie #archiemcgrowl #mistok #misericordiauniversity #mucareercenter #careers #mascottiktok #collegemascot ♬ original sound - Misericordia University Career & Networking Fairs Upcoming Fairs Fall 2026 Healthcare Career & Networking Fair - Friday, November 13, 2026 - 11:00am - 1:30pm Spring 2027 Career & Networking Fair - Friday, March 19, 2027 - 11:00am - 1:30pm More details can be found on Handshake . On-Campus Recruiting Options If you are interested in hosting an information table, an information session, or participating in on-campus interviews, please reach out to Janine Fawbush at jfawbush@misericordia.edu for more details. Healthcare Career Fair Highlights Check out our previous Healthcare Career Fair and see how students connected with employers and explored career pathways. Jobs and Internships Post on Handshake or attend recruitment events. Guaranteed Placement Program and Career Readiness Click for Career & Grad School Readiness Program Parent Information Help your student on the path to success! Student Government Association Misericordia SGA: Student-run board representing university students. Graduate School Resources Graduate and professional school assistance can be found here! Upcoming Events Click here Alumni on LinkedIn Click Here Career Outcomes Click Here Featured News Misericordia University Students Attend Family Service Association National Family Week Conference Dec 1 2025 9 : 37 AM Misericordia’s Insalaco Center for Professional Development and Leadership spon