arents & Families Institutes & Workshops Fun & Fitness Clinics & Centers Campus Store University Camps Other Offices Athletics Information For Future Students Parents and Families ROTC & Veterans Alumni (opens in new window/tab) Corporate Sponsors Donors Print Find It Fast Panel Close Panel Visit Apply Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Campus Map Search Clear Search About Directory (opens in new window/tab) myMU (opens in new window/tab) Athletics (opens in new window/tab) Map Jobs at MU Library Virtual Experience (opens in new window/tab) Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Upcoming Events All Events Sep 7 Labor Day (no classes) 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 30 PM N/A Oct 17 Open House all day Oct 19 Classes Resume; Second Subterm Begins 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 30 PM N/A Oct 26 Advisement Period 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 27 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 28 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Latest News More News Post RSS Feeds Subscribe to Post Alerts Misericordia University Dean Presents at tecBRIDGE Innovation Conference 9 / 4 / 2026 9 : 26 AM Misericordia University Bridge Program Helps First-Year Students Prepare for College Success 9 / 3 / 2026 1 : 04 PM Misericordia University Expands Nursing Pathways as Pennsylvania Addresses Workforce Shortage 9 / 2 / 2026 10 : 51 AM Misericordia University Celebrates Convocation and Welcomes the Class of 2030 8 / 28 / 2026 2 : 06 PM Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship 8 / 13 / 2026 10 : 03 AM Misericordia University Appoints Two New Members to Board of Trustees 7 / 30 / 2026 12 : 09 PM Admissions FAQ's More FAQ's What are the admission requirements? What type of financial aid is available? When should I apply? Who can I contact with questions about my application? What are the admission requirements? MU typically likes to see students with a history of proven success in the classroom with a minimum high school grade point average of 2.5. Minimum *SAT requirement is typically an 850 (Math + Critical Reading), but other factors can be taken into consideration. A number of programs have requirements for direct entry that are higher than university minimums. We advise checking the admission requirements for your program of interest within its designated section of the website. View our list of majors to find your program. *Note: Misericordia will be Test-Optional for Fall 2021 Admissions What type of financial aid is available? Misericordia offers merit-based scholarships for academics as well as community involvement, and need-based awards which can total well over $20,000 per year for qualified students. Visit our Financial Aid page to learn more . When should I apply? MU has a rolling admissions cycle, but we advise that students apply early in the cycle (Fall) as the space available in certain programs can be limited. Visit our Apply page to submit an application . Who can I contact with questions about my application? Your admissions counselor, or the Admissions Office at admiss@misericordia.edu or 1-866-262-6363. View our list of Admissions Staff to find your counselor. Parents Parents can access on-line resources and information useful for helping their student achieve professional success. Our staff is also available to answer questions on career options and career search. Misericordia University wants to open doors of opportunity for all of its graduates. The links below are some of the services most frequently asked about by parents. The Choice Program Guaranteed Placement Program Parent Guide to Career Development What Are Our Graduates Doing? Career Outcomes/Placement Statistics The Choice Program The Choice Program for Undeclared Students Misericordia University's Choice Program consists of a series of seven workshops designed to assist Undeclared students explore their interests, values, and skills as well as the various Misericordia major curricula and world of work. All incoming first year Undeclared students are encouraged to participate in this experience. During the seven-week series, students will complete a series of informal assessments, engage in individual and group reflection experiences, interact with area employers representing student's fields of interest, explore the Misericordia catalogue, and meet with Misericordia professors to explore career options in the various major fields. The Choice Program offers Undeclared students an opportunity to interact with other students who are exploring their futures and provides them with a support system as they adjust to college and make decisions about their major and career choices. This workshop series is co-facilitated by the Student Success Center and the Insalaco Center for Professional Development and Leadership. Guaranteed Placement Program Check out the GPP page to learn more. Parent Guide to Career Development In order for a student to become successful in a career after graduation, the student needs to have a plan. Parents can help with this plan by being a resource for their child and helping the student find other resources that he or she can utilize. Here are some ways to begin: Help your son/daughter develop a list of everyone you both know (friends, family, business associates, etc) that are working in your son/daughter's field of interest. Have your child contact these people to arrange an informational interview or a job shadowing experience where they can get a better understanding of the job and start building a network of professional contacts. If your son/daughter is not sure of their career path, encourage them to do internet research. The student should make a list of careers/occupations that interest them and research such things as the starting salary, the qualifications for this position and where the likely job markets are in the country for these positions. A good site for research is the Bureau of Labor Statistics Occupational Outlook Handbook . Encourage son/daughter to visit the Insalaco Center for Professional Development and Leadership to make an appointment. Our counselors can: Administer career aptitude assessments to help students find a career and a major that works for them Work with students to develop a resume and cover letter Practice interview skills Help students start their job search If you would like more information, a good book on this subject is “Parent's Guide to College and Careers: How to Help, Not Hover\" by Barbara Cooke. Students can take advantage of various workshops, mock interviews, career counseling and resume critiquing offered by the Insalaco Center for Professional Development and Leadership. In addition to these services, students can also search for internships and full-time/part-time jobs through our Misericordia Handshake site . The Insalaco Center maintains student-counselor confidentiality for all our sessions. It is our hope that parents will play a supportive role in their son's or daughter's career development process. What Are Our Graduates Doing? Check out where they are attending graduate school! Check out where they are working! Career Outcomes/Placement Statistics Career Outcomes (Class of 2024/2025) Gathered through the First Destination Survey at close of survey at 6-months post graduation Summary Total Graduates 557 Number of Responses 461 Knowledge Rate 83.0% Graduates - Undergraduate 367 Graduates - Graduate 190 Current Employment Status Overall Placement Rate 88.5% Employed Overall 57.7% Continuing Education 30.4% Still Looking (*at time of graduation, with no updated response at close of survey) 11.5% In Military 0.2% Not Seeking 0.2% Volunteering 0% Salaries Reported (Full-Time) Median Salary (173 responses) $75,000 $10,000 - $39,999 11.5% $40,000 - $59,999 16.2% $60,000 - $79,999 31.8% $80,000 + 40.5% Employment and Internships Guaranteed Placement Program (GPP) Upcoming Events Parents Student Government Association (SGA) Clubs and Organizations Graduate and Professional Resources Placement Statistics Misericordia University Founded by the Sisters of Mercy 301 Lake Street, Dallas , PA 18612 (570) 674-6400 Helpful Links Full-Time Undergraduate Online Programs Accelerated Degrees Jobs at MU Part-Time Graduate Open Houses Make a Gift to MU TikTok (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) Facebook (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Privacy Policy (opens in new window/tab) Site Map Accessibility Back to top Powered by Finalsite"
