vents Music Performance Pauly Friedman Art Gallery Parents & Families Institutes & Workshops Fun & Fitness Clinics & Centers Campus Store University Camps Other Offices Athletics Information For Future Students Parents and Families ROTC & Veterans Alumni (opens in new window/tab) Corporate Sponsors Donors Print Find It Fast Panel Close Panel Visit Apply Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Campus Map Search Clear Search About Directory (opens in new window/tab) myMU (opens in new window/tab) Athletics (opens in new window/tab) Map Jobs at MU Library Virtual Experience (opens in new window/tab) Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Upcoming Events All Events Sep 7 Labor Day (no classes) 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 30 PM N/A Oct 17 Open House all day Oct 19 Classes Resume; Second Subterm Begins 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 30 PM N/A Oct 26 Advisement Period 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 27 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 28 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Latest News More News Post RSS Feeds Subscribe to Post Alerts Misericordia University Dean Presents at tecBRIDGE Innovation Conference 9 / 4 / 2026 9 : 26 AM Misericordia University Bridge Program Helps First-Year Students Prepare for College Success 9 / 3 / 2026 1 : 04 PM Misericordia University Expands Nursing Pathways as Pennsylvania Addresses Workforce Shortage 9 / 2 / 2026 10 : 51 AM Misericordia University Celebrates Convocation and Welcomes the Class of 2030 8 / 28 / 2026 2 : 06 PM Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship 8 / 13 / 2026 10 : 03 AM Misericordia University Appoints Two New Members to Board of Trustees 7 / 30 / 2026 12 : 09 PM Admissions FAQ's More FAQ's What are the admission requirements? What type of financial aid is available? When should I apply? Who can I contact with questions about my application? What are the admission requirements? MU typically likes to see students with a history of proven success in the classroom with a minimum high school grade point average of 2.5. Minimum *SAT requirement is typically an 850 (Math + Critical Reading), but other factors can be taken into consideration. A number of programs have requirements for direct entry that are higher than university minimums. We advise checking the admission requirements for your program of interest within its designated section of the website. View our list of majors to find your program. *Note: Misericordia will be Test-Optional for Fall 2021 Admissions What type of financial aid is available? Misericordia offers merit-based scholarships for academics as well as community involvement, and need-based awards which can total well over $20,000 per year for qualified students. Visit our Financial Aid page to learn more . When should I apply? MU has a rolling admissions cycle, but we advise that students apply early in the cycle (Fall) as the space available in certain programs can be limited. Visit our Apply page to submit an application . Who can I contact with questions about my application? Your admissions counselor, or the Admissions Office at admiss@misericordia.edu or 1-866-262-6363. View our list of Admissions Staff to find your counselor. Clubs & Organizations Get involved, meet people, and build leadership skills outside the classroom. Misericordia offers a wide range of student clubs, special interest groups, communications, and SGA committees. Questions? Contact SGA at sgovern@misericordia.edu . How to Join Browse the lists below. Attend a meeting or event. Email SGA to connect with a leader. Contact SGA Search Clear Intramural Sports Want to compete, stay active, and have fun with friends? Intramurals are open to students of all skill levels. Check out what Intramural Sports are happening today! Student Clubs Get involved, build community, and explore your interests. Active Minds American Medical Student Association (AMSA) Autism Awareness Club Biology Club Colleges Against Cancer Dead Alchemist Society Education Club Government Law National Security (GLNS) Health Care and Management Association (HCMA) Math/Computer Science Club Special Interest Organizations Connect with peers around shared passions and causes. Adult Education Advisory Council (AEAC) Beyond Harmony Campus Peer Advocates College Democrats College Republicans Dance Ensemble Dance Team Mini-thon Club Misericordia Community Choir Misericordia ECO Reps Phi Theta Epsilon Sign Language Club Rotaract Ski and Snowboarding Club Student-Athlete Advisory Committee (SAAC) Tri Beta Yoga Club Student Communications Stay informed through student-led media and updates. The Highlander Newspaper Instress Literary Magazine Cougar Radio Station SGA Standing Committees Student-led groups that support campus programming and initiatives. Cougars Activity Council (CAC) Want to start a new club? Have an idea for a new organization? SGA can help you understand the process, requirements, and next steps. Email SGA to Get Started Misericordia University Founded by the Sisters of Mercy 301 Lake Street, Dallas , PA 18612 (570) 674-6400 Helpful Links Full-Time Undergraduate Online Programs Accelerated Degrees Jobs at MU Part-Time Graduate Open Houses Make a Gift to MU TikTok (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) Facebook (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Privacy Policy (opens in new window/tab) Site Map Accessibility Back to top Powered by Finalsite"
