imum *SAT requirement is typically an 850 (Math + Critical Reading), but other factors can be taken into consideration. A number of programs have requirements for direct entry that are higher than university minimums. We advise checking the admission requirements for your program of interest within its designated section of the website. View our list of majors to find your program. *Note: Misericordia will be Test-Optional for Fall 2021 Admissions What type of financial aid is available? Misericordia offers merit-based scholarships for academics as well as community involvement, and need-based awards which can total well over $20,000 per year for qualified students. Visit our Financial Aid page to learn more . When should I apply? MU has a rolling admissions cycle, but we advise that students apply early in the cycle (Fall) as the space available in certain programs can be limited. Visit our Apply page to submit an application . Who can I contact with questions about my application? Your admissions counselor, or the Admissions Office at admiss@misericordia.edu or 1-866-262-6363. View our list of Admissions Staff to find your counselor. Graduate Career Outcomes Career Outcomes (Class of 2024/2025) Gathered through the First Destination Survey at close of survey 6-months post-graduation Summary Total Graduates 557 Number of Responses 461 Knowledge Rate 83.0% Graduates - Undergraduate 367 Graduates - Graduate 190 Current Employment Status Overall Placement Rate 88.5% Employed Overall 57.7% Continuing Education 30.4% Still Looking (*at time of graduation, with no updated response at close of survey) 11.5% In Military 0.2% Not Seeking 0.2% Volunteering 0% Salaries Reported (Full-Time) Median Salary (173 responses) $75,000 $10,000 - $39,999 11.5% $40,000 - $59,999 16.2% $60,000 - $79,999 13.8% $80,000 + 40.5% Misericordia University Founded by the Sisters of Mercy 301 Lake Street, Dallas , PA 18612 (570) 674-6400 Helpful Links Full-Time Undergraduate Online Programs Accel